# Memory Protocol

Memory is useful only when it is short, factual, and relevant.

- Do not read every memory source at session start.
- Use repo code and current files as stronger evidence than old memory.
- Read `vault/**` only when the task names it or previous decisions are needed.
- Save memory only for durable facts: verified root cause, reusable command,
  project convention, or corrected stale knowledge.
- Never store secrets or unverified guesses.